# Literal spellings the name-interning constructors are handed on paths
# a job can re-enter, and why each site stands.
#
# Derived by tests/check-name-interning.sh: every call in src/lib that
# hands a string literal to xpost_name_cons, xpost_name_cons_n or
# xpost_name_cons_global, kept here only where the function holding it
# is one a job can re-enter -- reachable from an operator registration,
# from a function whose address is taken, or from xpost_run -- and is
# not itself installing operators. A site the walk clears runs only
# while machinery installs, which is the pattern these rows are held
# against: the font operators resolve their spellings once, in a table
# the installer walks (_op_font_names, src/lib/xpost_op_font.c), so a
# job's second ask for anything the machinery names allocates nothing.
#
# What a row is for. Interning a spelling the arena does not hold is a
# global allocation that lands wherever the first ask runs, so a
# literal on a job path is an allocation some job's own running may be
# first to make -- inside a measured stretch, on the one platform whose
# configuration reaches that site first. Each row says why that does
# not happen for its site: the spelling is interned while the world is
# built, or the site runs where devices are made and jobs are set up,
# before anything a job measures, or the first use of the feature pays
# and every ask after finds the name. A row is the site's answer, not
# its excuse: a site whose answer stops being true belongs in the
# installer's table, not here.
#
# disposition  file  function  spelling  reason
#
#   settled  the site stands, for the reason given
#   thorn    the site stands and the reason is a known irritation
#   heading  the site is expected to move where machinery installs

settled  xpost_dev_bgr.c       loadbgrdevice                .xpost_PPMIMAGE        the load operator's entry half: reaches the base class by the anchor the world build published (data/ppmimage.ps), and runs once as the device class loads
